    "type": "question",
    "label": "21",
    "prompt": "Solve the following. $$\\frac5{2x-1}-\\frac2{2x+1}=\\frac{2x}{4x^2-1}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=-\\frac74$",
      "worked": "The original denominators require $x\\ne-\\frac12,\\frac12$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{5(2x+1)-2(2x-1)}{(2x-1)(2x+1)}&=\\frac{2x}{(2x-1)(2x+1)}\\\\5(2x+1)-2(2x-1)&=2x\\\\6x+7&=2x\\\\4x&=-7\\\\x&=-\\frac74\\end{align*}$$\n\nThis value is permitted.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
